# Rebuilding px4-userland @VERSION@

This corresponding-source archive records repository commit `@COMMIT@` and
tree `@TREE@`. The `repository/` directory is the exact tracked source tree;
`third_party/libusb-1.0.28/` and its original verified source archive are the
libusb sources used for Android release binaries.

## Android rebuild and LGPL relink

Install Android NDK r27, CMake, Ninja, a POSIX shell, Python 3, Autoconf build
tools, and set `ANDROID_NDK_HOME` to the NDK root. From this archive root:

```sh
cd repository
scripts/build-android.sh \
  --abi arm64-v8a \
  --libusb-source ../third_party/libusb-1.0.28 \
  --output ../rebuilt-android-aarch64
scripts/build-android.sh \
  --abi armeabi-v7a \
  --libusb-source ../third_party/libusb-1.0.28 \
  --output ../rebuilt-android-armv7a
```

To relink with a modified LGPL libusb, modify a copy of
`third_party/libusb-1.0.28/` and pass that directory to `--libusb-source`.
The production release evidence path intentionally accepts only the pinned,
checksum-verified libusb source archive; local relink builds do not emit that
release evidence.

## Linux musl-dynamic rebuild

On x86_64 musl Linux, install CMake, Ninja, a C++17 compiler, shared libusb,
and pcsc-lite development headers, then run:

```sh
cmake -S repository -B build-linux -G Ninja \
  -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
  -DPX4_BUILD_TESTS=OFF \
  -DPX4_REQUIRE_PCSC_IFD=ON
cmake --build build-linux --target px4d px4-ts px4ctl px4_ifdhandler
```

## macOS arm64 rebuild

Install CMake, Ninja, Homebrew libusb, pkgconf, and Homebrew pcsc-lite. Export
their pkg-config paths, configure with the exact pcsc-lite include directory,
and build the CLIs and bundle:

```sh
pcsc_prefix="$(brew --prefix pcsc-lite)"
export PKG_CONFIG_PATH="$(brew --prefix libusb)/lib/pkgconfig:$pcsc_prefix/lib/pkgconfig"
cmake -S repository -B build-macos -G Ninja \
  -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
  -DPX4_BUILD_TESTS=OFF \
  -DPX4_REQUIRE_PCSC_IFD=ON \
  -DPX4_PCSC_IFD_INCLUDE_DIR="$pcsc_prefix/include/PCSC"
cmake --build build-macos --target px4d px4-ts px4ctl px4_ifd_bundle
```

The native products intentionally use host-provided shared libusb. Firmware
is neither required to compile nor present in this archive.
